+# MCP Versioning & Schema Evolution Plan
+
+Principles:
+- Always be backward compatible for GET/read operations. Make additive changes without breaking existing fields.
+- Use semantic versioning for API (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH). Increment MAJOR for incompatible breaking changes.
+- Schema stored with version metadata in each ModelContext record (schema_version).
+
+Developer workflow for schema changes:
+1. Propose change in PR with: OpenAPI diff, DB migration (Alembic), and adapter updates.
+2. Add new optional fields with defaults to remain backwards-compatible.
+3. If removing or renaming fields, implement a transitional adapter that maps both old and new fields for at least 1 release cycle.
+4. Update clients and bump MINOR API version for additive changes; announce deprecation schedule for removals.
+
+Data migration:
+- For structural DB changes, write Alembic migration scripts and include a reversible upgrade/downgrade path.
+- Run migrations in maintenance window; provide rollback plan.
+
+Subscriptions & eventing:
+- Event payloads include "schema_version" so subscribers can handle evolution.
+- Versioned webhook contract: subscribers may request a supported schema version at registration time.
+
